## Context
Child D of tracker 1045. The same checks run several times on nearly the same
content. Observed on PR 1557 (2026-10-21), from the seat reports: the coder's
`make check`, `/gaze`'s `make check` or targeted tests, the adherence seat's
`make lint` and tests, `/verify-gate`'s re-run of the targeted file, and the
forge's CI (10 jobs) on the branch, again on a second push, and on `main` after
the merge. Four or five runs per head, repeated every fix round. Wall time per
layer was not measured.

The forge ruleset `main-required-checks` was disabled by the author on
2026-10-21, but `.github/workflows/CI.yml` still runs on every push, so runners
are spent on a result nothing reads.

The one run that is not redundant is the one on the merge candidate commit
(`erg close`, a rebase onto a moved `main`, merge-time hook effects): that is
the gate record of child A (1156). Blocked by it, since the other skills can
read a result only once the record exists.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Measure first: wall time of each layer for one representative PR (coder,
      `/gaze`, adherence seat, `/verify-gate`, forge CI), written in the ticket
      log. The trim below is sized from that, not from this estimate.
- [ ] One authoritative full run: the child A gate on the candidate commit. Its
      record carries the result.
- [ ] `/gaze` and `/verify-gate` read the record, or the last result for the same
      tree, instead of re-running the full suite; each keeps a targeted run of the
      files the diff touches. A missing or stale record falls back to running the
      checks, never to skipping them.
- [ ] Coders run the scoped gate (`.idh-checks.json`) while working; the full run
      happens once.
- [ ] The forge workflow is trimmed to the jobs the local gate does not cover, or
      kept as a late safety net that nothing waits on, with the choice written
      down. Ask Fable before changing `CI.yml`.
- [ ] A negative control shows a stale record is not trusted (the tree changed
      after the record), and a positive control shows a fresh one is.
- [ ] Nothing here requires a particular agent runtime.
- [ ] Catalog regenerated and drift check clean; PR under the 15-file breaker,
      else split.
